# Content ↔ footer gap

Body content and the footer share **one** vertical rhythm token.

## Tokens (`:root` in `app/globals.css`)

- `--footer-top-gap` — footer shell inner `padding-top` (`.site-footer__shell`)
- `--content-footer-gap: var(--footer-top-gap)` — space from last body content to the footer’s top edge

Applied as:

```css
.site-main > main {
  padding-bottom: var(--content-footer-gap);
}
```

Never as margin on `.site-footer` / `.site-end` (outer footer margin caused canvas 露白).

## Rule

**Footer top padding = body→footer gap.** Same value on mobile and desktop. Change `--footer-top-gap` once → both sides update.

## Do not

- Zero out `main` `padding-bottom` on individual pages (home / about / services / etc.) to “meet” the footer
- Add a second footer-oriented bottom pad on the last section that stacks on top of `--content-footer-gap`
- Invent a page-local gap that differs from `--footer-top-gap`

Last sections may keep **internal** bottom padding for in-page rhythm only when it is clearly not the footer spacer; prefer `padding-bottom: 0` on the last band and let `main` own the footer air.

Known last-band zeros: `.svc-demo__stage:last-of-type`, `.home-page > .section.home-page__section:last-child`, `.about-content-sheet`, `.collection-detail__body`, `.faq-page`.
